# The rocker's keys are written to the kernel's gpio-keys device by hwinput (T-653): hidd reads them as from the rocker.
id: volume-keys
section: Media and sound
item: The hardware volume keys while a page plays sound: the media volume goes up and down with them and the sound keeps reaching the output sink; keyed down to nothing the sound reads muted, and heard again after
shells: enyo mochi mojo
prefs: jihad.media.autoplayWithSound=true
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-media-test.html?src=clip60av.webm&wide=1&sound=1
kit: cavekit-finger-testing.md R7
wait text status playing 20
# the first mark is what the run puts back at its end; then a known level, so the keys have room both ways
volume-mark
volume-set 44
expect sound heard 10 60 440
volume-mark
volume-key up 2
expect volume-hud
expect volume higher
expect sound heard 10 60 440
volume-mark
volume-key down 2
expect volume lower
expect sound heard 10 60 440
# the route muted: the volume keyed down to nothing. The sink still carries the tone, and "heard" cannot pass there
# (it wants the volume above 0): `expect sound muted` wants the tone at the sink AND the way out shut.
volume-key down 8
expect volume zero
expect sound muted 6 60 440
volume-mark
volume-key up 2
expect volume higher
expect sound heard 10 60 440
